<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`toml:fieldName[value]` keeps each input tiddler whose field `fieldName` reads exactly `value`, comparing as strings — the suffix names the field, the operand names the value. A carrier's TOML meta keys land as tiddler fields, so this operator queries the prelude directly: `[all[tiddlers]toml:heleuma[ka]]` gathers every carrier anchored at that mooring.

The comparison stays exact and stringly: a missing field reads as the empty string and matches only an empty operand.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/name-law>>

!! The Registered Name

TW5 binds a filter operator to its ''exported binding''. The export here reads `toml`, so the operator answers to `toml:…[…]` — the file name and the doc-comment reach nothing. Renaming the export renames the operator and unbinds every filter run that spelled the old name.

The module header inside the source carries the registration triple TW5 reads at boot — `title` (the `lar:` address), `type: application/javascript`, `module-type: filteroperator`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

